Setup Nexus and integrate with Jenkins :
1.update system package
#sudo apt-get update
2.Install openjdk 17 on ubuntu
#sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk openjdk-17-jre -y
3.Download the SonaType Nexus on ubuntu in /opt directory
#cd /opt
Open Sonatype's official download page: Sonatype Nexus Repository Downloads
Choose: Unix/Linux x86-64 | Nexus Repository 3.93.1
Then copy the actual download URL from the page and use wget on your EC2.
#wget https://download.sonatype.com/nexus/3/nexus-3.95.0-07-linux-x86_64.tar.gz.sha256

4.Extract the nexus repository setup in /opt directory
#tar -xvzf nexus-3.95.0-07-linux-x86_64.tar.gz

5.Rename the extracted nexus
#mv /opt/nexus-3.95.0 /opt/nexus

6.As security practice,  not to run nexus service using root user --> create new user as nexus to run nexus service
#sudo adduser nexus

7.To give permission to this user -->add user in the sudoers file
#visudo
nexus  ALL=(ALL) 	NOPASSWD: ALL

8.Give permission to nexus file and nexus directory to nexus user
#chown -R nexus:nexus /opt/nexus
#chown -R nexus:nexus /opt/sonatype-work

9.To run nexus as service at boot time , open /opt/nexus/bin/nexus.rc
#vi /opt/nexus/bin/nexus.rc
run_as_user="nexus"
save ":wq!"

10 nexus need more memory and more cpu to run but java does not assign by default this memory to nexus
So we need to tell this in nexus.vmoptions file
For this we add some values like-

-Xms1024m
-Xmx1024m
-XX:MaxDirectMemorySize=1024m
-XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions
-XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow
-Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true
-Dkaraf.home=.
-Dkaraf.base=.
-Dkaraf.etc=etc/karaf
-Djava.util.logging.config.file=etc/karaf/java.util.logging.properties
-Dkaraf.data=./sonatype-work/nexus3
-Dkaraf.log=./sonatype-work/nexus3/log
-Djava.io.tmpdir=./sonatype-work/nexus3/tmp

11.For a proper DevOps lab, don't manually start Nexus every time. Create a systemd service:

sudo vi /etc/systemd/system/nexus.service


[Unit]
Description=Nexus Repository
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=forking
LimitNOFILE=65536
User=nexus
Group=nexus
ExecStart=/opt/nexus/bin/nexus start
ExecStop=/opt/nexus/bin/nexus stop
Restart=on-abort

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

#systemctl start nexus
#systemctl status nexus

Nexus works on port number 8081
